<title>USA: Sikorsky sells four helicopters to Brazil.</title>
<headline>Sikorsky sells four helicopters to Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>STRATFORD, Conn. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sikorsky Aircraft, a unit of United Technologies Corp, said Monday that the Brazilian Army agreed to buy four S-70A Black Hawk helicopters.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Sikorsky said it will deliver the aircraft next month.</p>
<p>The company will also provide training and a five-year total maintenance program, including sending a support team to Brazil.  The Black Hawks will be based in Ecuador, and will fly military observation missions between Ecuador and Peru.</p>
<p>((--Hartford bureau, (860) 727-0224))</p>
